    },
    "body": "PR #1325/#1326 substantially improves learned geometric source selection: 103/119 correct payload reads and 83/119 correct emitted final answers on the retained construction. This review preserves that gain while correcting the proposed admission-first diagnosis. Of 1,813 reported positions, only 66 have an eligible target excluded from admission; another 217 occur among 608 omitted empty-pool positions. All present final queries are already covered, so full-stream admission utility must be measured before expanding the pool.\n\nThe next constructive task learns direct finite-action read influence with causal local-score observations, meaningful language fitting, matched categorical control and fixed full-stream denominators. The review also scopes reused evaluation data, refit attribution, causal controls, artifact binding, text interval reproducibility and actual continuation. README, active roadmap, evidence and handoff pointers are synchronized while historical artifacts/criteria remain preserved.\n\nValidation: six saved comparison intervals reproduce exactly; all 30 manifest files pass BLAKE3/size checks with zero unlisted files; sixteen text-document hashes and fit/evaluation disjointness verify; independent source, evidence and math reviews. Claim-wording, JSON parse, 850 local documentation links and git diff --check pass. Source/document/saved-data review only; no Rust build, model fit or inference. Storage 42.47 GB free against 36.77 GB reserve; no deletion or new model debit.\n\nReferences #820, #973, #1139, #962, #963, #964.\n",
